  "question": {
    "text": "If $f(x)=\\int \\frac{1}{x^{1 / 4}\\left(1+x^{1 / 4}\\right)} \\mathrm{d} x, f(0)=-6$, then $f(1)$ is equal to :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "zL9TQ",
      "text": "$4\\left(\\log _e 2-2\\right)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "dxOgD",
      "text": "$2-\\log _{e^2} 2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "RZFi6",
      "text": "$\\log _{\\mathrm{e}} 2+2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Co8ir",
      "text": "$4\\left(\\log _e 2+2\\right)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\text { Put } x^{1 / 4}=t \\Rightarrow d x=4 t^3 d t \\\\ & \\int \\frac{4 t^3 d t}{t(t+1)}=4 \\int\\left(\\frac{t^2-1}{t+1}+\\frac{1}{t+1}\\right) d t \\\\ & f(x)=4\\left[\\frac{x^{1 / 2}}{2}-x^{1 / 4}+\\ln \\left|x^{1 / 4}+1\\right|\\right]+C\\end{aligned}$\n$\\begin{aligned} & f(0)=-6 \\\\ & \\Rightarrow C=-6 \\\\ & \\Rightarrow \\quad f(1)=4\\left(\\log _e 2-2\\right)\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
